   "load_cycles": "Set -> end of blocking Wait = 7.7-7.96 us in loops; fitted 11700-12000",
   "switch_cycles": "unexplained time per switch 270-300 ns; fitted 400-500",
   "slots": "2: philox's last iteration reloads a chunk evicted one switch earlier",
   "fit_errors": "valu loops/straight within 0.5%; check (not fitted): philox_b1024x1024 (calib) -15.4% -> about -1%"
  },
  "scalar_phase3t": "smul.u32 -> sadd.s32 multiply-add chain: exactly 3.0 cycles per round (pop_scalar n=64/128/256 slope; the compiler schedules it in 2), so smul latency 2, sadd 1",
  "valu_latency_phase3v": {
   "vmin": "2: min_f32 chain 4.0 cycles/round (vmin + vadd 2)",
   "vand/vor/vclamps": "2 each assumed: round_clip round = 13 = vmul 2 + 2 vcvt 2 + vsel 1 + vand + vor + vclamps, so the three sum to 6",
   "vcmp": "eq_select also 3.0 cycles/round: vcmp <= 2, kept at 1"
  },
  "vector_queue_phase3u": "12 (11-13): pop_loop hides an 8-trip scalar inner loop under a 178-cycle MXU pop chain (in-order issue: +37%); 8 queued vadds after the pop stay hidden, 16 stall the front end",
  "sld_phase3wx": "sld load-to-use 6 cycles: phase3w loop variants (use 3/4/5 bundles after the load: +3/+2/+1 cycles) and phase3x unrolled pointer chases (6.0 cycles per load, straight-line and in loops; the compiler packs them 1-2 bundles apart). A 2-cycle address lag (H11) is refuted: +25-30% on the chases. sld_chain keeps 1 unexplained cycle per iteration.",
  "xpose_modes_phase3v": "short/narrow transposes (op text '(short)'/'(narrow)', width = last operand) queue all their results at .end: ceil(width/S) x ceil(rows/128) vregs (S 8 b32, 16 packed b16; rows = inputs x S; binary = two transposes), matching every Pallas kernel's vpop.trf count. result j at end + latency + j*interval. Fitted on phase3v xpose_chain r8 f32 / r16 bf16 (nv1 = latency sum; nv4 splits short vs narrow); narrow input occupancy <= 4 (f32 nv4: 2 and 4 give +0.3%, 8.22 gives +5.2%). Unannotated (full) transposes keep the phase3j per-input stream.",
  "xlane_warm_phase4": "cross-lane reductions issued within 48 cycles of the previous one on the same XLU return after 90 cycles, isolated ones after 104 (chains: vop_chain2 xmax/xsum 110/round, unit_chain). Fitted on attn_step phase4a-c: 35 -> 64 of 80 within 2%, median 3.0% -> 0.6%; chains unchanged."
